<title>UK: London platinum fixes at fresh 3-1/4 year low.</title>
<headline>London platinum fixes at fresh 3-1/4 year low.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of platinum was fixed at $358.50 an ounce on Wednesday afternoon, the lowest fixing since October 5, 1993.</p>
<p>It was fixed at $359.00 an ounce in the morning, and $362.25 on Tuesday afternoon.</p>
<p>Platinum has fallen sharply in recent days on the back of a sharp drop in the gold price. Dealers said the white metal was susceptible to losses down to $355 and then $350 an ounce.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 2936</p>
</text>
